# Materials Library — Single Source Of Truth

## Mandatory registration
Any **new SketchUp material name** (the material `display_name` used in SketchUp) that must participate in **indexed** PBR substitution, GLB export naming, or web-renderer lookup **must** be added to:

`na-apps/30__TrueVision__CoreAppCode/02__Src__AppModules/02__AppData/Na__AppConfig__MaterialsLibrary.json`
`https://www.noble-architecture.com/na-apps/30__TrueVision__CoreAppCode/02__Src__AppModules/02__AppData/Na__AppConfig__MaterialsLibrary.json`

The live URL mirrors the same path under `noble-architecture.com/na-apps/...`. Cousin projects (e.g. ValeVision3D) may hold a **copy** of this file; the **authoritative** file for new entries is the NaWeb TrueVision CoreAppCode path above unless the team explicitly migrates ownership.

Do **not** invent ad-hoc material names in Ruby exporters, hardware JSON, or renderer code without a matching library entry.


## Naming convention
- Format: `MAT{NNN}__{Category}__{Variant}...` — **three digits** after `MAT`, then `__`.
- `SketchUpName` in JSON **must** match the SketchUp material display name **exactly** (character-for-character).
- The runtime treats names matching `/^MAT\d{3}__/` as indexed materials (`Na__MaterialsSystem__IsIndexedName`).


## Series layout (high level)
- **MAT000** — defaults / template  
- **MAT100** — basic (glass, wood, mirror, etc.)  
- **MAT300** — paint  
- **MAT500** — timber  
- **MAT600** — metals: generic / galvanised / structural / aluminium (**MAT600–MAT603**), **MAT604–MAT610 reserved**, ironmongery finishes from **MAT611** (Chrome, Brass, Bronze, SatinNickle token for MAT614).

New metals or ironmongery finishes: extend `MAT600__MetalSeries__` following existing keys; assign the next free code; document in `meta.seriesNotes` when adding a new band.


## Workflow for new materials
1. Choose the next **MAT###** code and full `SketchUpName` string.  
2. Add an entry under the correct series object; inherit from `MAT001__Default` behaviour — only specify keys that differ from defaults.  
3. Create or rename the SketchUp material so its name matches `SketchUpName`.  
4. Bump `meta.version` and `meta.lastUpdated` when the file changes.  
5. If a mirror exists (e.g. ValeVision3D), sync the same JSON or re-copy from NaWeb.

